<body style="height: auto; min-height: auto;">Ref No: {{{Case.Case_Number__c}}}<br />
<br />
Hi {{{Case.First_Name__c}}},<br />
<br />
Thank you for getting in touch regarding your experience at our Qantas Club/our Business/First/Partner Lounge- at {{{Case.Departure_Airport__c}}} airport on {{{Case.Email_Departure_Date_Time__c}}}.<br />
<br />
<strong>Things don’t always go to plan</strong><br />
<br />
We want every departure to be smooth and enjoyable, so I was sorry to hear that you were incorrectly denied you entry into the Qantas Club/our Business/First/Partner Lounge - I understand your disappointment.<br />
<br />
I wanted to assure you that our airport management in {{{Case.Departure_Airport__c}}} have been made aware of the error and will be discussing this with the staff on duty that day to make sure they are following our policies.<br />
<br />
<strong><em>-If a Frequent Flyer:-</em></strong><br />
<br />
As a gesture of goodwill, I’ve credited {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to your Frequent Flyer account.<br />
<br />
<br />
<em><strong>-If not a Frequent Flyer: -</strong></em><br />
<br />
As a gesture of goodwill, I’d like to arrange a credit of {{{Case.Recovery_Quantity__c}}} Qantas Points to you.<br />
<br />
Please can you let me know your Frequent Flyer number by replying to this email so I can credit points to your account. If you’re not already a member you can use this&nbsp;<a href="https://www.qantas.com/en-au/frequent-flyer/join/code/familyfree">link</a>&nbsp;to join free of charge.<br />
<br />
<strong>We value your opinion&nbsp;</strong><br />
<br />
Customer feedback plays an important role in our continuous improvement process so that we can provide you with exceptional service from start to finish.<br />
<br />
I want to assure you that I’ve passed your feedback on to the relevant team for review.<br />
<br />
Thank you for taking the time to tell us about your experience, I hope we deliver an exceptional service next time you fly with us.<br />
<br />
&nbsp;</body>
</html>